{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom functools import reduce\n\nprimes = [p for p in range(2, 6000) if all(p % q != 0 for q in range(2, p))]\n\ndef factor(n):\n    d = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            c = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                c += 1\n            d[p] = c\n    if n > 1:\n        d[n] = 1\n    return d\n\ndef divisors(n):\n    return reduce(\n        lambda divs, pe: [d * pe[0] ** k for d in divs for k in range(pe[1] + 1)],\n        factor(n).items(),\n        [1]\n    )\n\ndef process(n, m):\n    f = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        f[i] = 2 * f[i - 1]\n        for x in divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= x <= i:\n                f[i] += f[i // x] - f[(i - 1) // x]\n                f[i] %= m\n        f[i] %= m\n    return f[n]\n\nn, m = [int(x) for x in input().split()]\nprint(process(n, m))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\n// Precompute primes up to 6000\nvector<int> get_primes() {\n    vector<int> primes;\n    for (int p = 2; p < 6000; ++p) {\n        bool is_prime = true;\n        for (int q = 2; q * q <= p; ++q) {\n            if (p % q == 0) {\n                is_prime = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (is_prime) primes.push_back(p);\n    }\n    return primes;\n}\n\n// Factorize n using the given primes list\nvector<pair<int, int>> factor(int n, const vector<int>& primes) {\n    vector<pair<int, int>> factors;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) break;\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int cnt = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                ++cnt;\n            }\n            factors.push_back({p, cnt});\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) {\n        factors.push_back({n, 1});\n    }\n    return factors;\n}\n\n// Generate all divisors from prime factorization\nvoid gen_divisors(const vector<pair<int, int>>& factors, int idx, int current, vector<int>& divs) {\n    if (idx == (int)factors.size()) {\n        divs.push_back(current);\n        return;\n    }\n    int p = factors[idx].first;\n    int e = factors[idx].second;\n    int pow = 1;\n    for (int k = 0; k <= e; ++k) {\n        gen_divisors(factors, idx + 1, current * pow, divs);\n        pow *= p;\n    }\n}\n\nvector<int> divisors(int n, const vector<int>& primes) {\n    vector<pair<int, int>> fac = factor(n, primes);\n    vector<int> divs;\n    gen_divisors(fac, 0, 1, divs);\n    return divs;\n}\n\nlong long process(int n, int m, const vector<int>& primes) {\n    vector<long long> f(n + 1);\n    f[0] = 0;\n    f[1] = 1;\n    f[2] = 2;\n    for (int i = 3; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long val = (2 * f[i - 1]) % m;\n        vector<int> divs = divisors(i, primes);\n        for (int x : divs) {\n            if (x >= 2 && x <= i) {\n                long long diff = f[i / x] - f[(i - 1) / x];\n                diff = (diff % m + m) % m; // ensure non-negative\n                val = (val + diff) % m;\n            }\n        }\n        f[i] = val % m;\n    }\n    return f[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<int> primes = get_primes();\n    long long result = process(n, m, primes);\n    cout << result << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.4638240878121e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0002083561266772449, -0.00047791501856409013, -1.156323378381785e-05, -0.062056463211774826, -1.4781842764932662e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.25537464022636414, -0.048636384308338165, -0.02324696071445942, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.04115801304578781, -0.3869020342826843, -0.002285608323290944, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -9.846202738117427e-05, -0.35692161321640015, -0.441713809967041, -0.0004544417606666684, -0.0004677870310842991, -4.0531076592742465e-06, 0.0, -1.823885577323381e-05, -0.0019306369358673692, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.13087336719036102, -0.004103930201381445, -0.000912250077817589, 0.0, -0.7200330495834351, -0.018152184784412384, 0.0, -0.5826801061630249, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.008880051784217358, -0.12692835927009583, 0.0, -0.00023100091493688524, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006679587997496128, -1.8954096958623268e-05, 0.0, -0.00035482310340739787, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0005584587925113738, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -0.006716651376336813, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.318072337307967e-06, -0.03374950587749481, -0.0005553610390052199, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.000566203030757606, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.0